    "title": "📅 Nobel Laureate Daron Acemoglu to give virtual lecture April 8 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "12 hours ago Virginia Tech will host Nobel Prize-winning economist Daron Acemoglu for the 2026 Philosophy, Politics, and Economics Distinguished Public Lecture on April 8 from 5 to 6:30 p.m. The event will be held online via Zoom , and advance registration is required .\nAcemoglu, a professor at MIT, will discuss modern technological and economic change and the role of liberalism — themes from his upcoming book Remaking Liberalism . The lecture is organized by the David H. Kellogg Center for Philosophy, Politics, and Economics in the College of Liberal Arts and Human Sciences .\nThe annual series brings leading thinkers to share insights at the intersection of politics, economics, and philosophy. Past speakers have included Amartya Sen, Ester Duflo, and Adam Tooze.\nMore Info: Nobel Prize winner, economics professor to speak a...",
